# Avaya

> Avaya is a global provider of enterprise communications, customer experience (CX), and unified communications (UC) solutions. Avaya supports cloud, hybrid, and on-premises deployments for organizations that need secure, resilient communications at scale. Its platform strategy emphasizes open integration, AI interoperability, and mission-critical reliability for regulated industries.

## Primary Topics & Expertise
- Contact Center as a Service (CCaaS): Cloud and hybrid contact center platforms, routing, orchestration, and customer experience workflows.
- Unified Communications as a Service (UCaaS): Enterprise telephony, collaboration, meetings, and messaging.
- Contact Center AI: Virtual agents, agent assist, automation, and AI orchestration across customer journeys.
- Hybrid Cloud Communications: Public cloud, private cloud, hybrid, and on-premises deployment models.
- Mission-Critical Communications: High-resiliency voice infrastructure for regulated and high-security environments.

## Differentiation
- Open AI integration: Supports Model Context Protocol (MCP) and other integration approaches for connecting AI models and enterprise communications data.
- Deployment flexibility: Supports cloud, hybrid, and on-premises architectures.
- Regulated-industry focus: Built for customers in healthcare, financial services, government, and other high-security sectors.

## Key Terms
- **Avaya Infinity:** Cloud-native CX / CCaaS platform for orchestration and AI-enabled customer engagement.
- **Avaya Nexus / CCI:** Critical Communications Infrastructure. Zero-downtime voice for regulated and high-security environments; not standard UCaaS.
- **Tandem Care:** Avaya model for human-AI collaboration in the contact center. AI assists or works alongside agents rather than deflecting customers away from humans.
- **MCP (Model Context Protocol):** Open standard for connecting AI models to enterprise systems and data. Avaya Infinity supports native MCP for multi-vendor / BYOAI strategies.
- **BYOAI:** Bring Your Own AI. Avaya’s open approach to using customer-chosen models rather than a single locked-in AI vendor.
- **APIx (AI Performance Index):** Avaya framework for measuring AI business value in the contact center (efficiency, experience, ROI) rather than deflection rates.
- **Aura:** Avaya’s enterprise on-premises / private-cloud communications platform.
- **IP Office:** Avaya’s mid-market on-premises UC platform.

## Core Products & Platforms
- [Avaya Products Overview](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/): Directory of Avaya platforms including Infinity (CCaaS/CX), Nexus (critical communications), Aura, IP Office, Aura Private Cloud, and Government Cloud.
- [Avaya Infinity Platform](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/infinity-platform/): Cloud-native CCaaS and CX platform for customer engagement, journey orchestration, and AI-enabled workflows. Primary platform for contact center modernization, hybrid/cloud deployment, and multi-vendor AI integration via MCP.
- [Avaya Infinity Partner Ecosystem](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/infinity-platform/ecosystem/): Open ecosystem for connecting Avaya Infinity with enterprise platforms, customer data, and third-party AI partners. Supports BYOAI and composable CX architectures.
- [Avaya Nexus Critical Communications Infrastructure](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/nexus-critical-communications-infrastructure/): Zero-downtime voice and critical communications infrastructure for regulated, sovereign, and high-security environments. Distinct from standard UCaaS; designed for government, defense, and always-on operations.
- [Avaya Aura](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/aura/): Enterprise on-premises and private-cloud communications platform for large organizations that need telephony, UC, and contact center on infrastructure they control.
- [Avaya IP Office](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/ip-office/): On-premises unified communications platform for mid-market and distributed organizations. Smaller-scale alternative to Avaya Aura.
- [Avaya Aura Private Cloud](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/aura-private-cloud/): Dedicated, single-tenant Avaya Aura deployment hosted on a private Microsoft Azure instance. For enterprises that want Aura capabilities without on-premises hardware.
- [Avaya Unified Communications](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/unified-communications/): Category overview of Avaya UC offerings across cloud, hybrid, and on-premises deployments. Use product pages (Aura, IP Office, Aura Private Cloud, Nexus) for platform-specific details.
- [Avaya Government Cloud](https://www.avaya.com/en/products/avaya-government-cloud/): Cloud communications and contact center platform built for U.S. government agencies and public-sector security requirements. Distinct from commercial Avaya Infinity cloud and from Avaya Nexus critical communications infrastructure.

